            <ArticleTitle>Sharp, left-sided back pain · bilateral leg weakness · degenerative disc disease · Dx?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 84-year old woman came to the emergency department with sharp back pain on her left side that she'd had for 4 days. The pain radiated to her posterior hips when standing. She said her whole body felt achy and she was experiencing weakness in both legs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
